                "With THIL's total credit envelope established at $100,000,000—comprising $32,000,000 in fund-based working capital, $48,000,000 in non-fund-based facilities, and an additional $20,000,000 in Long-Term Capex Term Debt—Titan National Bank cannot absorb the entire exposure alone. Under central bank Large Exposure Framework (LEF) limits, a commercial bank's single-borrower exposure is capped at 20% of its Tier-1 capital base. Furthermore, prudent risk governance dictates syndicated risk distribution. Titan National Bank therefore triggers a formal 4-Bank Consortium Syndication.",
                "The Consortium Syndication Structure: Titan National Bank acts as the Mandated Lead Arranger (MLA) and Facility Agent, underwriting 40% of the aggregate facility ($40,000,000). The MLA syndicates the remaining 60% across three peer commercial banks: (1) Apex Commercial Bank takes a 25% allocation ($25,000,000); (2) Crestline Capital Bank takes a 20% allocation ($20,000,000); and (3) Vanguard Industrial Bank takes a 15% allocation ($15,000,000). Each member bank participates across all three tranches (Fund-Based Working Capital, Non-Fund-Based Limits, and Capex Term Debt) on a strictly pro-rata basis.",
                "Pari-Passu Charge Creation & Security Trustee Architecture: To secure the $100M total exposure, the consortium creates a unified collateral perimeter. Under Indian and Anglo-American corporate law, individual banks do not hold separate, fragmented mortgages over specific factory buildings or inventory bins. Instead, the consortium appoints an independent corporate trustee, 'Apex Security Trustee Ltd.', to hold all security on trust for the benefit of the four consortium lenders. The collateral package comprises: (1) A First Pari-Passu Floating Charge over all present and future Current Assets of THIL (raw materials, work-in-progress, finished inventory, book debts, and operating bank balances); and (2) A First Pari-Passu Fixed Mortgage over all immovable properties, industrial factory land, heavy plant equipment, and machinery located at THIL's manufacturing headquarters.",
